The semiconductor industry is investing in increasingly sophisticated wafer-fabrication processes to support advanced logic, memory and AI computing devices. These processes require precise wafer positioning, stable thermal conditions and reliable handling inside manufacturing equipment. Electrostatic chucks (ESCs) are important components in this environment because they use electrostatic forces to hold wafers securely during selected semiconductor processing operations.

